{
  // MONEY-1118 item 13 — type-check the TESTS too.
  //
  // `tsconfig.json` includes only `src/**/*`, so none of the 62 files under
  // `__tests__/` ever saw `tsc`. That is not cosmetic: a missing required field
  // in a test fixture surfaced as a RUNTIME failure instead of a compile error,
  // and on another occasion two helper functions sat defined-but-never-called
  // in a test file with nothing to catch them.
  //
  // A separate config rather than widening `include`, because the main one
  // EMITS: it sets `rootDir: "./src"`, `outDir: "./dist"` and
  // `declaration: true`, so pulling `__tests__` in would either fail with
  // "not under rootDir" or start emitting .d.ts files for test code into dist.
  // This one only checks.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    // Widened to the MONOREPO root, not this package.
    //
    // `__tests__` sits outside src/, so the inherited `rootDir: "./src"` had to
    // go. Pointing it at "." (this package) then broke on a test that imports
    // the real `normalizeQuarter` from packages/research by relative path — its
    // comment explains why it wants the genuine article rather than a
    // hand-copied constant, and it is right to: the whole point is asserting
    // BSE and NSE key a quarter identically.
    //
    // `@usemoney/research` is not a dependency of core and does not export that
    // module, so importing it by package name is not available either, and
    // adding the dependency would point core at a package that already depends
    // on core.
    //
    // rootDir exists to control the LAYOUT OF EMITTED OUTPUT. This config emits
    // nothing (`noEmit: true` above), so there is no layout to constrain and
    // widening it costs nothing. tsconfig.json still emits with
    // `rootDir: "./src"`, unchanged.
    "rootDir": "../..",
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,

    // OFF for tests only. base.json enables it, and it produced 78 of the 79
    // errors this config first surfaced — every one an `arr[0]` on a
    // known-shape fixture. Neither failure item 13 was filed about is an
    // indexed access:
    //
    //   "a missing required field in a test fixture surfaced as a RUNTIME
    //    failure instead of a compile error"
    //   "two helper functions sat defined-but-never-called in a test file"
    //
    // Keeping it on would mean 78 non-null assertions added to assertions —
    // noise that buys nothing, and `!` sprinkled through tests is how a real
    // narrowing bug later hides in the crowd. In a test, indexing past the end
    // of a fixture already fails the test, which is the same signal.
    //
    // src/ is UNAFFECTED: tsconfig.json still checks it with the flag on.
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false

    // NOT enabling `noUnusedLocals`, despite it being item 13's second
    // motivation (two helpers defined-but-never-called in a test file).
    // Compiler options are per-PROJECT, not per-file, so it cannot be aimed at
    // `__tests__` alone: turning it on reported 5 unused symbols in `src/`
    // (getBrokerEnvKeys, normalizeColumnName, seriesGroupCount, CRUMB_TTL_MS,
    // BACKOFF_BASE_MS) and one in `packages/datadog`. Those look like real dead
    // code and are worth removing — but that is a dead-code sweep across two
    // packages, not "type-check the tests", and bundling it here would make
    // this config's failure mode confusing.
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "__tests__/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
